WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.840
Nearly 330,000 people are displaced as Yemeni forces leave the Red Sea Street to defend Aidan. This is Omni View Top World News, Episode 55. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. After this, a third American carrier in the Middle East, a fresh peak in U.S. gas exports, and a night of killings in South Africa, then a dispute over a European bank merger and a sign of progress. Sundays pull out from Dubab Airport and the Babel Mandab.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:33.980
The southern armed forces told the BBC is meant to reinforce Aidan and the governorates

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.320
around it after weeks of heavier fighting with the Iran-backed Houthis.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.260
Houthi-run media say those fighters now hold the ground the troops left, and Saudi Arabia

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.200
has not commented.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:47.960
The shift ends in offensive along a route the Houthis took in a September surprise attack.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.800
The pro-government side said it had secured the strait in early October, and the Houthis

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.220
said they had already taken Purim Island and the port of Mocha a month before that claim.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:01.500
regime. Those fighters said commercial ships in the waterway were not their target, but

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.420
Saudi vessels were, and losing that overlook helped push oil prices up, because Riyadh

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.340
had been exporting through the Red Sea after the United States and Israel's war with

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:11.360
Iran shut Hormuz.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:17.120
Ravena Shondasani, for UN human rights, urged every party to spare civilians and civilian

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:21.520
buildings, and said women and children were more than 60 percent of documented civilian

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:22.840
casualties since August.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:28.900
Houthis struck Aiden's presidential palace on 15 October, killing five and injuring 16.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:32.020
Saudi Arabia answered with hundreds of airstrikes.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.160
The Houthis sent hundreds of drones and missiles at Saudi cities.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.200
Hundreds of people are reported killed.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:43.060
The war dates to the Houthis' 2014 seizure of Sana'a and a Saudi-led intervention in 2015.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.920
And a four-year informal ceasefire started coming apart in July when the Houthis declared

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.000
a maritime embargo on Saudi Arabia.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.222
A U.S. official told Al Jazeera the carrier Theodore Roosevelt reached the Middle East

00:01:55.222 --> 00:02:00.382
on Monday, a third American flat top beside the George Washington and the George H.W. Bush

00:02:00.382 --> 00:02:01.942
inside Central Command's area.

00:02:02.502 --> 00:02:05.262
The Pentagon and Central Command have not confirmed that arrival.

00:02:05.842 --> 00:02:09.962
A separate official said the ship got there on the 15th of November, after leaving San

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:10.982
Diego in September.

00:02:11.482 --> 00:02:16.262
Washington and Tehran had a two-week ceasefire in April, and a wider memorandum in June

00:02:16.262 --> 00:02:21.402
that collapsed in early July, and mediators from Pakistan and Qatar have been trying to stop a return

00:02:21.402 --> 00:02:26.902
to the march exchanges that hit the wider Gulf. Talks to end the U.S.-Israel war on Iran for good,

00:02:27.362 --> 00:02:32.602
and to reopen Hormuz are still stalled. Last week President Donald Trump said further strikes were

00:02:32.602 --> 00:02:37.282
quite unlikely, and that the military part of the war was effectively over after he spoke with

00:02:37.282 --> 00:02:42.642
Qatar's Prime Minister, Sheikh Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Jassim Al-Thani, and he added that

00:02:42.642 --> 00:02:45.542
that U.S. forces stay locked and loaded if conditions change.

00:02:46.002 --> 00:02:51.262
The Navy says the Roosevelt, commissioned in 1986, carries more than 5,000 people and

00:02:51.262 --> 00:02:54.122
more than 60 aircraft, including F-18s.

00:02:54.502 --> 00:02:58.822
A U.S. official told Al Jazeera last month that the Mac and Island group, with more than

00:02:58.822 --> 00:03:03.322
2,000 Marines, had also headed that way, and the Wall Street Journal put a possible

00:03:03.322 --> 00:03:08.362
added total at 9,000 to 10,000 U.S. soldiers, which the military has not confirmed.

00:03:08.362 --> 00:03:16.197
Pipeline gas into every American-liquified natural gas export plant hit about 21.8 billion cubic feet on Saturday.

00:03:16.757 --> 00:03:22.317
Energy Connects reported from Bloomberg NEF, an all-time high and more than 12 percent above a year ago.

00:03:22.897 --> 00:03:27.677
Golden Pass took a record volume that day, and Sabine Pass saw it strongest flow since April.

00:03:28.297 --> 00:03:36.037
The extra cargoes could ease Europe and Asia as winter starts, after the Middle East War sent buyers hunting supply and lifted prices to the highest in years.

00:03:36.037 --> 00:03:41.017
Asian prices in the region that imports the most have tripled from pre-war levels,

00:03:41.257 --> 00:03:43.857
and European gas futures are up nearly threefold.

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:47.417
US export output is poised to double by the end of the decade.

00:03:47.877 --> 00:03:51.277
The international energy agency still expects a glut in the coming years,

00:03:51.677 --> 00:03:55.817
but Persian Gulf disruptions have pushed that oversupply back by at least two years.

00:03:56.848 --> 00:04:02.048
Police in South Africa are investigating 17 murders in two Sunday night shootings they say are not

00:04:02.048 --> 00:04:06.588
linked. The BBC reported. Eight men were killed in a minibus outside Peter

00:04:06.588 --> 00:04:11.488
Maritzburg in Quazulunital. Spokesperson Robert Netcciunda said officers

00:04:11.488 --> 00:04:15.168
found a white seven-seater full of bullet holes, and that neither the motive

00:04:15.168 --> 00:04:19.348
nor the suspects' names were established. Hours later, in the Jeffsville

00:04:19.348 --> 00:04:23.808
settlement at Adderidgeville, west of Pretoria, police found six men and three

00:04:23.808 --> 00:04:27.248
women dead inside a four-room shack between 10 and 11 at night.

00:04:27.788 --> 00:04:31.348
Bodies across the rooms and spent cartridges outside. Brigadier

00:04:31.348 --> 00:04:36.048
Brenda Muradili said Gauteng's provincial commissioner had sent crime intelligence and a tracking

00:04:36.048 --> 00:04:36.448
team.

00:04:37.028 --> 00:04:38.748
Neighbors first took the shots for thunder.

00:04:39.148 --> 00:04:43.688
The country is struggling to contain violent crime, including gang killings, and has one

00:04:43.688 --> 00:04:45.128
of the world's highest murder rates.

00:04:45.628 --> 00:04:50.828
In September, eight gunmen killed 18 people at a bar near Johannesburg on the 25th,

00:04:50.828 --> 00:04:55.348
with 14 injured, and the next day, 10 people were killed outside of venue near Cape Town,

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:56.528
with 11 injured.

00:04:56.528 --> 00:05:00.888
Much of that violence is tied to gang turf wars over drugs and illegal mining.

00:05:01.348 --> 00:05:06.168
In February, President Cyril Remaphosa called organized crime the most immediate threat

00:05:06.168 --> 00:05:09.088
to democracy, society, and economic development.

00:05:09.528 --> 00:05:13.568
The military went out with police earlier this year in the five provinces with the highest

00:05:13.568 --> 00:05:18.728
murder rates, including Gauteng, and in January five men were shot dead in daylight outside

00:05:18.728 --> 00:05:20.288
a shop in that Pretoria area.

